{"code":"geocoach-canada-metas","tips":[{"id":"geocoach-canada-metas-378","section":"Alberta bollard","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=Hm1EkjGPUvZs7bvIXdeGfQ&viewpoint=49.52350026658997%2C-112.08191922284976&heading=319.46976582402874&pitch=-12.22458505114821","text":"The Alberta bollard is mostly white, with the top having a \"black-white-black\" pattern.","countryCodes":["CA"],"sourceTagId":"378"},{"id":"geocoach-canada-metas-379","section":"Alberta highway","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=AqHDLZYVYqT5ABo4CSszUg&viewpoint=53.71664620369254%2C-114.17537847940604&heading=35.16683750713951&pitch=-3.1223726789855135","text":"Alberta highway signs can have one of two layouts, however both of them will say \"Alberta\" at the top.","countryCodes":["CA"],"sourceTagId":"379"},{"id":"geocoach-canada-metas-380","section":"British Columbia guardrails","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=aNRfalZ_4wkrPoR7_i0ywA&viewpoint=49.8905892944012%2C-120.32758795855027&heading=329.439264711771&pitch=-1.7788084184635693","text":"In British Columbia, it is common to find concrete barriers instead of guardrails","countryCodes":["CA"],"sourceTagId":"380"},{"id":"geocoach-canada-metas-381","section":"British Columbia Highway","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=ZZ5MnY5vHHodhkiWJOOyXA&viewpoint=50.60313067049456%2C-119.15358071667958&heading=22.01085297784784&pitch=1.2838432445633003","text":"Highway signs in British Columbia can have one of two designs, in both cases they will usually say \"B.C.\" at the bottom.","countryCodes":["CA"],"sourceTagId":"381"},{"id":"geocoach-canada-metas-382","section":"British Columbia Maximum","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=1cJye3ZNmKU1kxQSX04Qvg&viewpoint=49.509174162619495%2C-115.7760121248074&heading=93.4523506962826&pitch=-2.9301387335552107","text":"In British Columbia, the Maximum sign will often say \"km/h\" at the bottom in black text.","countryCodes":["CA"],"sourceTagId":"382"},{"id":"geocoach-canada-metas-383","section":"Manitoba bollard","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=27wR2tZuE5QKmsarDzUjOw&viewpoint=50.72740693818133%2C-101.02013923307898&heading=266.82492868342064&pitch=-10.42616776256429","text":"The Manitoba Bollard is white, with the top of it being black and there being an orange band further down. The version without an orange sticker can be found in Saskatchewan too for example.","countryCodes":["CA"],"sourceTagId":"383"},{"id":"geocoach-canada-metas-384","section":"Manitoba signpost sticker","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=TBEDjHphA2Z06mGeptuicQ&viewpoint=50.432375144567104%2C-99.4700487555333&heading=190.62299195630317&pitch=-6.371248283965713","text":"Signposts in Manitoba can have a green/white striped sticker on them.","countryCodes":["CA"],"sourceTagId":"384"},{"id":"geocoach-canada-metas-385","section":"Manitoba highway","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=1XXCKIo2Ww4Ja1rHpmsvQA&viewpoint=49.98990785639657%2C-100.46205049814796&heading=140.31509542639594&pitch=-4.604371665312215","text":"Manitoba highway signs have 2 designs, however both of them will say \"Manitoba\" in green text at the top.","countryCodes":["CA"],"sourceTagId":"385"},{"id":"geocoach-canada-metas-386","section":"New Brunswick highway","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=qxXiyNUnAwWo2uPsG7D54A&viewpoint=46.969056837750955%2C-65.71642863203661&heading=193.36374427958947&pitch=-3.250660371827877","text":"New Brunswick highway signs will include \"NB\" as well as the shape of New Brunswick.","countryCodes":["CA"],"sourceTagId":"386"},{"id":"geocoach-canada-metas-387","section":"New Brunswick Stop + Arrêt","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=olHgqD2seGfs4cQIJwqrBg&viewpoint=47.624803391938904%2C-65.67738310961032&heading=287.4373808452288&pitch=-0.2785901829104773","text":"A lot of stop signs in New Brunswick will say both Stop and Arrêt on the same sign.","countryCodes":["CA"],"sourceTagId":"387"},{"id":"geocoach-canada-metas-388","section":"Newfoundland fire hydrant diamond","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=rY0qBYOus6RQPQxh_cIKqw&viewpoint=47.545365431400704%2C-52.75109921097605&heading=302.17399401958573&pitch=-12.059015133243436","text":"On the island of Newfoundland, fire hydrants will often have a pole with a diamond-shaped marker next to them.","countryCodes":["CA"],"sourceTagId":"388"},{"id":"geocoach-canada-metas-389","section":"Newfoundland and Labrador highway","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=RX7-jIiHNJ3vo5nsaqDv4A&viewpoint=48.51066914354465%2C-58.271075866134886&heading=218.52892115168345&pitch=1.8469508101462253","text":"Highways in Newfoundland and Labrador will be a white rectangle with the number inside, they will often also say \"ROUTE\" on a green background above it","countryCodes":["CA"],"sourceTagId":"389"},{"id":"geocoach-canada-metas-390","section":"Newfoundland and Labrador Pyramid","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=SzNXJr0cKz468a0Sca5CuQ&viewpoint=48.55267289456277%2C-58.52723412331304&heading=357.59441605240323&pitch=-13.730953737434035","text":"In Newfoundland and Labrador you can find these wooden poles with a pyramid shaped top on guardrails.","countryCodes":["CA"],"sourceTagId":"390"},{"id":"geocoach-canada-metas-391","section":"Newfoundland and Labrador T-intersection","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=82k4tL1zJlaGI0hbkR0XFA&viewpoint=48.51005861410317%2C-58.27141628857356&heading=279.1757487175023&pitch=1.5734896230251252","text":"In Newfoundland and Labrador, intersections will often have this sign.","countryCodes":["CA"],"sourceTagId":"391"},{"id":"geocoach-canada-metas-392","section":"Newfoundland and Labrador wooden box","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=KpEr48leKPc9sOl5BLr48g&viewpoint=47.94770683625207%2C-53.95143338040588&heading=132.96253736273863&pitch=-10.293818120156288","text":"In Newfoundland and Labrador, you can find these wooden boxes holding a sign inside them.","countryCodes":["CA"],"sourceTagId":"392"},{"id":"geocoach-canada-metas-393","section":"Nova Scotia brown highway","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=C9z1YE5rpy9FE0sAu4ottA&viewpoint=44.37149248705038%2C-64.74102534354478&heading=206.41402203526047&pitch=-4.085575467066832","text":"The brown highways in Nova Scotia have a very simple design. The design is just a brown rectangle with the highway number.","countryCodes":["CA"],"sourceTagId":"393"},{"id":"geocoach-canada-metas-394","section":"Nova Scotia Highway Shield","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=4_7heK_ZVUYzI3rs66Ezrw&viewpoint=44.37260954865559%2C-64.97325436042547&heading=223.33749734184855&pitch=2.3548564279421385","text":"One version of the highways in Nova Scotia resembles the highway shield of the US highways.","countryCodes":["CA"],"sourceTagId":"394"},{"id":"geocoach-canada-metas-395","section":"Nova Scotia blue highway","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=xUxOXUF10SO4EYoIsihFyA&viewpoint=45.106459740597266%2C-63.41287458667097&heading=48.91218435747866&pitch=0.09673423323772568","text":"The blue highway sign in Nova Scotia will also feature the flag of Nova Scotia.","countryCodes":["CA"],"sourceTagId":"395"},{"id":"geocoach-canada-metas-396","section":"Northwest Territories highway","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=bQRUqYkO3CWbWNsIN6IIyg&viewpoint=60.557479997846976%2C-116.14024519223524&heading=172.6026600744224&pitch=-1.9073480777842633","text":"Highway signs in the Northwest Territories can be easily identified by the \"NWT\" that is on the sign,","countryCodes":["CA"],"sourceTagId":"396"},{"id":"geocoach-canada-metas-397","section":"Ontario diamond","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=soW49pECik7vFyeGOJrZlQ&viewpoint=44.826223510040656%2C-79.32205080641594&heading=34.21091314600954&pitch=-7.554524792365399","text":"In Ontario you can find these diamond shaped markers on the side of the road. The colors can vary but they will often be green/white.","countryCodes":["CA"],"sourceTagId":"397"},{"id":"geocoach-canada-metas-398","section":"Ontario highway","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=LOar4ZSiL6574IJS_IL9nw&viewpoint=46.13349921910651%2C-80.43167444113118&heading=56.16986766586697&pitch=-0.11604079933211152","text":"Highway signs in Ontario look like this, one main way to identify them is that most designs feature a crown on them or say \"Ontario\".","countryCodes":["CA"],"sourceTagId":"398"},{"id":"geocoach-canada-metas-399","section":"Ontario Maximum","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=UH2J0EoOdRa9vK-b69kvrw&viewpoint=44.24974369563453%2C-77.43512700276358&heading=97.3780657767601&pitch=-1.0758372095799444","text":"Similarly to British Columbia, the Maximum signs in Ontario can say \"km/h\" at the bottom, however in Ontario this will be written in white text on a black background.","countryCodes":["CA"],"sourceTagId":"399"},{"id":"geocoach-canada-metas-400","section":"Prince Edward Island highway","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=0PqmiDLmQM6IwemYXqOMOg&viewpoint=46.42537778951069%2C-63.57042312598538&heading=22.010810205613712&pitch=0.8350516048517846","text":"On Prince Edward Island, highway signs can be identified easily with the trees at the top of the sign,","countryCodes":["CA"],"sourceTagId":"400"},{"id":"geocoach-canada-metas-401","section":"Quebec Arrêt","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=GeLNkHfyMUMhDl16IP0gFA&viewpoint=49.221048124169755%2C-68.15096456755614&heading=261.10278919894097&pitch=-0.8994423021969027","text":"Stop signs in Quebec will say \"Arrêt\".","countryCodes":["CA"],"sourceTagId":"401"},{"id":"geocoach-canada-metas-402","section":"Quebec bollard","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=F5UpgQ2kBNLBRica3W0MUg&viewpoint=46.573060959757576%2C-71.99284648276495&heading=66.00132010466126&pitch=-0.6230522821532105","text":"In Quebec, you can find these bollards with a red or green reflector at the top. They will only be seen on guardrails.","countryCodes":["CA"],"sourceTagId":"402"},{"id":"geocoach-canada-metas-403","section":"Quebec highway","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=Tf6W2QGRoGWaICrIgL7JGQ&viewpoint=46.08104588791608%2C-72.46472978514457&heading=240.85751155345184&pitch=9.765867101998836","text":"Highway signs in Quebec can be blue or green, both of them will feature the Fleur-de-lis symbol (pic 2).","countryCodes":["CA"],"sourceTagId":"403"},{"id":"geocoach-canada-metas-404","section":"Saskatchewan highway","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=zBtYBeRQy3UcYfTgbVjcAg&viewpoint=49.87301663563136%2C-106.95954611378868&heading=134.2610799214702&pitch=-2.616538703955797","text":"Highway signs in Saskatchewan can by identified by their unique symbol, in one design it will be in the center, while on others it will be at the top 3 times.","countryCodes":["CA"],"sourceTagId":"404"},{"id":"geocoach-canada-metas-405","section":"Saskatchewan Triangles","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=4HUVZyCvKRJHjR-LPxqUUA&viewpoint=53.159908282421874%2C-105.76167252729695&heading=32.17234406279048&pitch=-2.0410185662043006","text":"Signposts in Saskatchewan can have these white triangles attached to them. The number can vary.","countryCodes":["CA"],"sourceTagId":"405"},{"id":"geocoach-canada-metas-406","section":"Yukon-highway","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=YSsi8adx8VYf-qU_fU-i_A&viewpoint=60.81001582388621%2C-135.20879781019192&heading=132.16126350201614&pitch=-6.699605198748699","text":"Highway signs in Yukon will always have a square with a colored outline and white inside, with the road number written in the middle in the same color as the outline. The color can be red or green.","countryCodes":["CA"],"sourceTagId":"406"}]}